      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "We've seen a lot of discussion about the new Quick Menu layout, and we get it: when familiar buttons move, muscle memory takes the hit.\n\nThis layout change is part of a broader shift to bring Events and Groups closer to the center of the VRChat experience. Surfacing what's happening live helps more players discover and join experiences together, which is a big focus for us right now.\n\nRight now, this layout is part of an ongoing experiment. We're testing how changes like this affect how people navigate and discover social experiences in VRChat. We need to see how it performs at scale once it's live before deciding what sticks and what needs another pass.\n\nFeedback is a key part of that process, as is data, A/B testing, etc. What you share here helps us spot friction that metrics alone can't capture. We'll be watching feedback closely after launch as well, and the results of both player sentiment and data will guide what comes next.\n\nbtw: the old \"expando\" button (which some folks have mentioned) and the new \"Live Now\" button both open the same place. They go to the main menu's hub for events and worlds (which used to be launchpad, and is now Live Now). That's why we removed the little expando guy, it's duplicate behavior",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    },
